# Code owners.
#
# This file is real ownership metadata for the repository, and it is also the
# input the policy engine reads when a quarantine recommendation needs an owner.
# Without it, every recommendation falls back to "last committer to the file",
# which is a guess -- so the demo showed `unresolved` and the fallback path was
# never exercised against a real declaration.
#
# The last matching rule wins, which is GitHub's own precedence and what
# flaketriage.policy.ownership implements.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @Kuber-code

# The deterministic core. A bug here is wrong output, not a worse suggestion,
# which is why it is held to a higher coverage floor than the classifier.
/src/flaketriage/detect/     @Kuber-code
/src/flaketriage/identity/   @Kuber-code
/src/flaketriage/policy/     @Kuber-code

# The evaluation harness and its corpus. Changes here move published numbers, so
# they warrant the same scrutiny as changes to the thing being measured.
/eval/                  @Kuber-code

# Design records are append-mostly; editing a shipped ADR rewrites history.
/docs/adr/              @Kuber-code

# Thresholds are behaviour. A change to this file changes what the tool decides
# without changing a line of code.
/flaketriage.toml       @Kuber-code
